    Taking a real-valued frequency signal and bringing it into the time domain
    gives Hermitian symmetric output:

    >>> t = torch.linspace(0, 1, 5)
    >>> t
    tensor([0.0000, 0.2500, 0.5000, 0.7500, 1.0000])
    >>> T = torch.fft.ifft(t)
    >>> T
